---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — Free QR Code Generator" description="Our privacy commitment: zero upload, zero cookies, zero tracking of QR content. We explain exactly what data is and isn't collected.">
  <section class="container" style="padding: 2rem 0;">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Nothing about your QR code content.</strong> All generation happens in your browser. Your URLs, WiFi passwords, vCards, and other inputs never leave your device.</p>
    <h2>What we use</h2>
    <p>We use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which records aggregated page views without cookies or personal identifiers. We never see your IP address or fingerprint.</p>
    <h2>Short URL Service</h2>
    <p>If you choose to shorten a long URL using the "Shorten URL" button on the URL tab, we receive that long URL. We store the mapping (a randomly generated 6-character id pointing to your long URL) so that the short link works. We do not log your IP address, User-Agent, or Referer. The only data we collect for short links is a click count, which is incremented each time the short link is followed.</p>
    <p>To request deletion of a short link, email us at the address on the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page. We will remove the mapping from our database within 7 days. The QR tool itself remains 100% client-side: no QR content you generate is sent to us unless you explicitly click the "Shorten URL" button.</p>
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>The site displays ads served by Google AdSense. Google may set cookies for ad personalization. You can opt out via <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">Google's ad settings</a> or use an ad blocker.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? See our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
